# A fader ride on strip 1 of an X-Touch in MC mode, as the MCU reference
# describes the messages: touch note 104, pitch bend on channel 0 while
# touched, release.
#
#   > surface to bridge          < bridge to surface (since the last check)
#   ! command the bridge sends   @ delta faderz sends
#   + n                          n milliseconds pass
#   several messages on one < line are separated by commas

# A move before the touch is an echo: nothing is written.
> e0 00 60
! none
# The first frame moves every motor to the state: strip 1 closed, the
# master to the program bus at 0 dB.
< e0 00 00, e8 7f 5f
> 90 68 7f
! touch /channels/ch1/fader
+ 25
> e0 7f 5f
! set /channels/ch1/fader 0
# Two moves within 20 ms: only the later goes out, when the interval ends.
+ 5
> e0 00 58
+ 5
> e0 00 50
! none
+ 20
! set /channels/ch1/fader -5
# No motor move while the fader is held, whatever faderz says.
@ {"changes": [{"path": "/channels/ch1/fader", "value": -12}]}
< none-of e0
> 90 68 00
! release /channels/ch1/fader
# Let go: the motor goes to the value shown, the last one written
# (-5 dB is 10239 of 16383).
+ 25
< e0 7f 4f
